' pi-mono-java source baseline: 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873
' Design repository baseline: 3fa6eb57c40b1af599dd495db916eaa360e3638d
' Source evidence: modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/Agent.java:60-61,218-268, VIRTUAL_THREAD_EXECUTOR and startExecution
' Source evidence: modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/loop/AgentLoop.java:209-276, invokeModel and consumeStream
' Source evidence: modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/tool/ToolExecutionPipeline.java:178-207, executeSequentially and executeInParallel
' Source evidence: modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/openai/OpenAIResponsesProvider.java:113-175, doStream and executeStream
' Source evidence: modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/stream/EventStream.java:14-27,54-88, EventStream
' Observed behavior: agent runs, provider readers, and parallel tool calls already use virtual threads.
' Java divergence: current event buffering is unbounded and current code has no deployment-level run admission.
' Target-only design: HTTP acceptance, SSE recovery, leases, bounded queues, and the 100-run profile are proposed additions.
' Design reason: separate execution, capacity, persistence, and delivery lifetimes so each can fail and recover independently.
' Product constraint: the review target is 100 active agent runs in an agreed deployment scope.
' Security hardening: immutable run context and bounded low-cardinality telemetry prevent cross-session leakage.

@startuml http_sse_virtual_thread_dfx_overview
title CampusClaw HTTP and SSE Virtual-Thread DFX Overview

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Internal HTTP Client" as Client
participant "HTTP Resource API" as Http
participant "Runtime Health Gate" as Health
participant "Run Capacity Manager" as Capacity
queue "Bounded PendingRun Queue" as Queue
database "RuntimeSessionStore" as Store
participant "Virtual-Thread Executor" as Executor
participant "Agent Loop" as Loop
participant "Downstream Gates" as Gates
participant "Model / Tool / Attachment" as Services
database "Bounded Run Event Journal" as Journal
participant "SSE Adapter and Byte Budget" as Sse

Client -> Http : POST idempotent run request
Http -> Http : authenticate, validate, and deduplicate
Http -> Health : check admission state
Health --> Http : OPEN or PRESSURE
Http -> Capacity : acquire count and weighted bytes

alt capacity is immediately available
  Capacity --> Http : idempotent RunLease
else bounded queue has item and byte capacity
  Capacity -> Queue : enqueue immutable PendingRun
  note over Queue
    No run virtual thread or
    downstream lease exists yet.
  end note
  Queue --> Http : RunLease before timeout
else queue is full, timed out, or shedding
  Capacity --> Http : admission rejected
  break request rejected before acceptance
    Http --> Client : 429 or 503 with bounded retry hint
  end
end

Http -> Store : atomically persist message, run, and idempotency result
Store --> Http : accepted run identifier
Http --> Client : 202 Accepted
Http -> Executor : dispatch accepted run with reconciliation
Executor -> Loop : start one new virtual thread

note over Executor, Loop
  One accepted run owns one new virtual thread.
  Virtual threads are not pooled or reused.
end note

loop model and tool turns until terminal
  Loop -> Gates : acquire only the current phase lease
  Gates -> Services : bounded model, tool, or content call
  Services --> Gates : event, result, or failure
  Gates --> Loop : release phase lease
  Loop -> Journal : append bounded typed event with run sequence
end

Loop -> Store : persist terminal state first
Store --> Loop : terminal committed
Loop -> Journal : append terminal event
Loop -> Capacity : close RunLease exactly once

Client -> Sse : GET events with Last-Event-ID
Sse -> Journal : read snapshot and subscribe after cursor
Journal --> Sse : ordered event stream
Sse --> Client : SSE id equals run sequence

break subscriber is slow or disconnects
  Sse --> Client : close only this subscription
  note over Loop, Sse
    The accepted run continues independently.
  end note
end

note over Health, Sse
  Cross-cutting DFX: metrics, traces, JFR pinning, tenant fairness,
  immutable run context, graceful shutdown, and state reconciliation.
end note
@enduml
